---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, pricing } from '../site.config';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What happens in the trial lesson?',
    a: "We go through your previous scores and where you lost marks, I hear you speak, and we look at your writing. You'll leave knowing which criteria are holding you back and how long it will realistically take to reach your target.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you teach Academic or General Training?',
    a: 'Both. Speaking and Listening are the same in both versions, and the Writing Task 2 essay works the same way. Where they differ, mainly Writing Task 1 and Reading, we prepare for the version you are sitting.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long will it take to get from 6 to 7?',
    a: "It depends on where you're losing marks and how much you practise between lessons. Some students move quickly once the technique clicks: Durant reached 7.5 in two months. In the trial I'll give you a realistic estimate, not a sales promise.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Where do lessons happen?',
    a: 'Online, one-to-one, by video call. You can join from anywhere in the world.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What time zone are you in?',
    a: "I'm based in the UK. When you book, available times show in your own time zone automatically.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you guarantee my score?',
    a: "No, and be wary of anyone who does. What I can promise is that you'll know exactly what's costing you marks, and you'll have a method to fix it.",
  },
];

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'EducationalOrganization',
    name: site.name,
    url: site.url,
    description: site.description,
    founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: site.tutor, jobTitle: 'IELTS tutor' },
    sameAs: [site.instagram, site.tiktok],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
    })),
  },
];
---

<Base title="IELTS Tutor for Band 7 Speaking and Writing" schema={schema}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">IELTS Speaking &amp; Writing coaching</p>
      <h1>Stuck at Band&nbsp;6? Your English isn't the&nbsp;problem.</h1>
      <p class="lede hero__lede">
        You hold conversations, write emails and get through your day in English. Then test day comes and the score
        won't move. I teach you exactly what examiners reward in Speaking and Writing, so your next attempt is your last.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/book">Book a trial lesson</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/book#ask">Ask a question first</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero__meta">One-to-one, online · Academic and General Training</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Proof strip -->
  <section class="proof" aria-label="Student results">
    <div class="wrap proof__inner">
      <div class="proof__stat">
        <span class="proof__num">7.5</span>
        <span>Durant's band, two months after starting lessons</span>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="proof__quote">
        <p>"I still remember the PEE method she taught me when I was feeling very confused before taking the IELTS."</p>
        <cite>Cynthia</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problem -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why your score won't move</p>
        <h2>Band 7 isn't better English. It's English an examiner can&nbsp;score.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The examiner isn't asking whether you can communicate. You can. They're scoring you against fixed criteria,
          and Band 6 answers miss them in predictable ways.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2 gaps">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Answers that stop too soon</h3>
          <p>You answer the question, then go quiet. Band 7 speakers develop the point without being pushed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Ideas that go nowhere</h3>
          <p>In Writing Task 2 you state a position and move on. The marker wants it explained and supported.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Safe vocabulary</h3>
          <p>
            The same words you use every day. Band 7 needs less common words used naturally, not memorised
            "advanced" phrases dropped in at random.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Grammar that plays it safe, or breaks</h3>
          <p>
            You either avoid long sentences or they fall apart halfway. Band 7 needs a range of structures, mostly
            error-free.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="narrow closer">
        Every retake costs another test fee and another few weeks. If nothing changes in how you prepare, nothing
        changes in the result. More English won't fix this. <strong>Technique will.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Method -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="method">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we work on</p>
        <h2>All four papers. Built around the two that hold you&nbsp;back.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Speaking and Writing are where a human examiner judges how you use English, and they're where most Band 6
          candidates lose their marks. That's where most of our time goes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--3 gaps">
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <p class="tag">Main focus</p>
          <h3>Speaking</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>The PEE method (Point, Explain, Example), so you stop running dry after one sentence</li>
            <li>Planning a Part 2 long turn in the 60 seconds you're given</li>
            <li>Handling abstract Part 3 questions without freezing</li>
            <li>Fewer fillers, natural linking and clear pronunciation</li>
            <li>Speaking with confidence, mistakes and all</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <p class="tag">Main focus</p>
          <h3>Writing</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Task 2: answering the exact question, with a clear position throughout</li>
            <li>Paragraphs that develop one idea properly instead of listing five</li>
            <li>Linking ideas without stuffing in "Furthermore" and "Moreover"</li>
            <li>Task 1: a clear overview and the features that matter</li>
            <li>Feedback on your writing against the official band descriptors</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="tag tag--quiet">Strategy</p>
          <h3>Reading &amp; Listening</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Timing, so you finish every section</li>
            <li>Techniques for the question types that cost you most</li>
            <li>Spotting the traps: paraphrase, distractors and spelling</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>Diagnose. Fix. Repeat until it holds.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <span class="steps__n">1</span>
          <h3>Trial lesson</h3>
          <p>
            We find exactly where your marks are going. You leave knowing your weakest criteria and what it will take to
            fix them.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="steps__n">2</span>
          <h3>A plan for your test date</h3>
          <p>
            Lessons target your gaps, not a generic syllabus. If your test is close, we start with what moves the score
            fastest.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="steps__n">3</span>
          <h3>Practice until it's automatic</h3>
          <p>
            Technique only counts if it survives exam pressure. We drill it until you use it without thinking, so it's
            still there on test day.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Results -->
  <section class="section section--dark" id="results">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Results</p>
      <h2>What happens when the technique clicks</h2>
      <div class="results">
        <div class="result result--stat">
          <span class="result__num">7.5</span>
          <p><strong>Durant</strong> reached Band 7.5 within two months of starting lessons.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="result result--quote">
          <blockquote>
            <p>
              "I am very pleased to have met Teacher Moona online. She is extremely patient and highly effective in her
              teaching methods. I still remember the PEE method she taught me when I was feeling very confused before
              taking the IELTS. It helped enrich my sentences and made speaking less difficult when I was often stuck.
              Many of her other methods are also very practical.
            </p>
            <p>
              At first, I was always too afraid to speak in oral exams, but Teacher Moona constantly encouraged me to
              speak, saying that it was okay to make mistakes. Gradually, speaking became less challenging, and
              eventually, I achieved a satisfactory IELTS score."
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption><strong>Cynthia</strong> · IELTS 6.5</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap about">
      <div class="about__photo">
        {
          site.photo ? (
            <img src={site.photo} alt="Moona, IELTS tutor" width="420" height="525" loading="lazy" />
          ) : (
            <div class="about__placeholder" aria-hidden="true">M</div>
          )
        }
      </div>
      <div class="about__text">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your tutor</p>
        <h2>Hi, I'm Moona.</h2>
        <p>
          I'm a TEFL-certified English tutor based in the UK, and I've coached hundreds of students online through the
          hardest parts of learning English.
        </p>
        <p>
          After enough Band 6 students, I saw the same problems come up again and again: strong English, weak exam
          technique. The methods I teach were built to fix exactly those problems, and they're simple enough to use
          under pressure.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm patient, and I'll push you to speak, mistakes and all. That's usually where the breakthrough happens.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/book">Book a trial lesson</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who it's for -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Is this for you?</p>
        <h2>This is for people who need the score, not just the practice.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2 gaps">
        <div class="card fit fit--yes">
          <h3>A good fit if</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You need Band 7 or above for a visa, a university place or professional registration</li>
            <li>You've sat IELTS at least once and missed your target</li>
            <li>Your everyday English is good, but your score doesn't show it</li>
            <li>You want honest feedback, not reassurance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card fit fit--no">
          <h3>Not the right fit if</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You're a beginner or lower intermediate learner</li>
            <li>You want a guaranteed band score. Nobody can honestly promise one</li>
            <li>You'd rather watch a course than practise out loud</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing -->
  <section class="section" id="pricing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Lessons</p>
        <h2>Start with a trial. Decide after.</h2>
        <p class="lede">All lessons are one-to-one by video call. Times show in your own time zone when you book.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--3 gaps">
        {
          pricing.map((p) => (
            <div class={`card price ${p.featured ? 'price--featured' : ''}`}>
              {p.featured && <p class="tag">Best value</p>}
              <h3>{p.name}</h3>
              <p class="price__amount">{p.price}</p>
              <p class="price__length">{p.length}</p>
              <ul>
                {p.points.map((pt) => (
                  <li>{pt}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
              <a class={`btn ${p.featured ? 'btn--primary' : 'btn--ghost'}`} href="/book">
                {p.cta}
              </a>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2>Before you book</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        {
          faqs.map((f) => (
            <details>
              <summary>{f.q}</summary>
              <p>{f.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>Ready to find out what's holding your score back?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Book a trial lesson. You'll leave with a clear diagnosis and a plan, whether or not you carry on with me.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row cta__buttons">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/book">Book a trial lesson</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/book#ask">Ask a question first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: clamp(72px, 12vw, 140px) 0 clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 15ch;
  }
  .hero__lede {
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .hero__meta {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .proof {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .proof__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px);
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 28px;
    padding-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .proof__stat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 320px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .proof__num {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 3.25rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  .proof__quote {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: clamp(0px, 5vw, 64px);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .proof__quote p {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }
  .proof__quote cite {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .grid--2 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }
  .grid--3 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }
  .gaps {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 28px;
  }
  .card p:last-child,
  .card ul:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .card ul {
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .card li {
    margin-bottom: 0.55em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .card--feature {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent);
  }
  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .tag--quiet {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
  }
  .closer {
    margin-top: 40px;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 40px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .steps li {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }
  .steps__n {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .steps p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .results {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .result {
    background: #332e2a;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 32px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .result--stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }
  .result__num {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(5rem, 12vw, 7.5rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .result p {
    color: #e8e1d7;
  }
  .result--quote blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .result--quote blockquote p {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .result figcaption {
    color: #bfb6aa;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .result strong {
    color: var(--bg);
  }

  .about {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 380px) 1fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .about__photo img,
  .about__placeholder {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .about__placeholder {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 6rem;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  .about__text p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .about__text .btn {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .fit h3 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .fit ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .fit li {
    padding-left: 1.75em;
    position: relative;
  }
  .fit li::before {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .fit--yes li::before {
    content: '✓';
    color: #3d7a4a;
  }
  .fit--no li::before {
    content: '✕';
    color: #a3402b;
  }

  .price {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .price--featured {
    border-color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--ink);
  }
  .price .tag {
    align-self: flex-start;
  }
  .price__amount {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
    margin: 8px 0 4px;
  }
  .price__length {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .price ul {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .price .btn {
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .faq {
    margin-top: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 20px 40px 20px 0;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.075rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  summary::after {
    content: '+';
    position: absolute;
    right: 4px;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  details[open] summary::after {
    content: '−';
  }
  details p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .cta {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cta .narrow {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .cta__buttons {
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .grid--3,
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .results {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .grid--2,
    .about,
    .proof__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .proof__quote {
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 20px 0 0;
    }
    .about__photo {
      max-width: 320px;
    }
  }
</style>
